From: William Floyd <git@notmy.space>
Date: Mon, 8 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add manual focus controls

Snapshot has no manual controls at all today, which issue #215 asks for:
cameras get focus and exposure wrong often enough that being able to pin
them down matters. This adds the focus half, on top of the camera control
API in aperture.

A camera that reports both AfMode and LensPosition gets a button in the
controls bar opening a popover with a Manual Focus switch and a position
slider. Everything else is unchanged: a camera exposing neither -- a
fixed-focus front sensor, most webcams -- gets no button at all rather
than a control that moves nothing.

The slider is in the units LensPosition is specified in, dioptres, which
are the reciprocal of the focus distance. That is not a number anyone
wants to read, so the ends are marked "Far" and "Near" and the value
itself is not drawn.

Two details come from how the underlying control works:

  - Controls are silently discarded while a camera is idle, so the
    popover follows the viewfinder in and out of Ready. The camera and
    the state are separate properties that settle in either order, so it
    is driven from both notifications rather than from the state alone.

  - Dragging a slider emits value-changed continuously, and each change
    makes the camera re-settle before it trusts its own sharpness
    measurement again. Positions are therefore coalesced to at most one
    per 50ms, always the most recent, with the final position guaranteed
    to be sent when the drag ends.

Because controls cannot be read back, the slider starts from the
controls

